{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:asymptotic-ray","title":"def:asymptotic-ray","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":310,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#def:asymptotic-ray","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-ray]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"def:asymptotic-ray","line":530,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Asymptotic rays]\n\\label{def:asymptotic-ray}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:minimizing-geodesic-ray, def:minimizing-geodesic-window}\n\n\n\n\n\nLet $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$ be minimizing rays in a metric space. The ray\n$\\mu$ is \\emph{asymptotic to $\\lambda$} if there are $t_n\\to\\infty$\nand minimizing segments from $\\mu(0)$ to $\\lambda(t_n)$ which converge\nto $\\mu$ uniformly on compact subsets of $[0,\\infty)$. Their domains\nexhaust $[0,\\infty)$ because\n$d(\\mu(0),\\lambda(t_n))\\ge t_n-d(\\mu(0),\\lambda(0))$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Asymptotic rays] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a6173796d70746f7469632d726179\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">morgan-tian</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aminimizing-geodesic-ray\">↗ def:minimizing-geodesic-ray</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aminimizing-geodesic-window\">↗ def:minimizing-geodesic-window</a> <p></p>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda $\">$\\lambda $</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mu $\">$\\mu $</span> be minimizing rays in a metric space. The ray <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mu $\">$\\mu $</span> is <em>asymptotic to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda $\">$\\lambda $</span></em> if there are <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$t_n\\to \\infty $\">$t_n\\to \\infty $</span> and minimizing segments from <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mu (0)$\">$\\mu (0)$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\lambda (t_n)$\">$\\lambda (t_n)$</span> which converge to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\mu $\">$\\mu $</span> uniformly on compact subsets of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[0,\\infty )$\">$[0,\\infty )$</span>. Their domains exhaust <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$[0,\\infty )$\">$[0,\\infty )$</span> because <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d(\\mu (0),\\lambda (t_n))\\ge t_n-d(\\mu (0),\\lambda (0))$\">$d(\\mu (0),\\lambda (t_n))\\ge t_n-d(\\mu (0),\\lambda (0))$</span>. ","warnings":[]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-along-ray","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-ray","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-ray","label":"def:minimizing-geodesic-ray"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:minimizing-geodesic-window","title":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window","label":"def:minimizing-geodesic-window"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","title":"lem:asymptotic-ray-exists","label":"lem:asymptotic-ray-exists"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:asymptotic-ray","title":"lem:asymptotic-ray","label":"lem:asymptotic-ray"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#cor:asymptotic-ray-busemann-bound","title":"cor:asymptotic-ray-busemann-bound","label":"cor:asymptotic-ray-busemann-bound"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one","title":"lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one","label":"lem:busemann-gradient-norm-one"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#line","title":"line","label":"line"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:asymptotic-ray","title":"def:asymptotic-ray","tex":"\\begin{definition}[Asymptotic rays]\n\\label{def:asymptotic-ray}\n\n\\source{morgan-tian}\n\\uses{def:minimizing-geodesic-ray, def:minimizing-geodesic-window}\n\n\n\n\n\nLet $\\lambda$ and $\\mu$ be minimizing rays in a metric space. The ray\n$\\mu$ is \\emph{asymptotic to $\\lambda$} if there are $t_n\\to\\infty$\nand minimizing segments from $\\mu(0)$ to $\\lambda(t_n)$ which converge\nto $\\mu$ uniformly on compact subsets of $[0,\\infty)$. Their domains\nexhaust $[0,\\infty)$ because\n$d(\\mu(0),\\lambda(t_n))\\ge t_n-d(\\mu(0),\\lambda(0))$.\n\\end{definition}","source":"tex/references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","description":